================================================================================
PATH 2 C1: MPI-decompose the ENERGY2/GPUPOT O(N^2) potential at ADJUST
================================================================================
Date     : 2026-06-10
Branch   : mpi-parallel
Binary   : GPU2/run_versions/nbody7b.mpi-cpu  (pure-MPI, OMP_NUM_THREADS=1)
Harness  : run_phase_attr.sh (N=5e4 matrix), run_equiv.sh (bit-identity)
Baseline : results_phase_attribution_2026-06-10.log (Step 0, pre-C1)

WHAT CHANGED
  GPU2/lib/gpupot.cpp   : + gpupot_range(i0,ni,n,m,x,pot) -- evaluates the
    potential only for the i-slice against the FULL j-set; the j-loop is a
    verbatim copy of gpupot()'s (same order, same compensated float
    summation) so pot[i] is bit-identical to the full evaluation. gpupot()
    itself untouched (serial path = shipped instruction stream).
    + extern "C" gpupot_range_ Fortran binding (1-based i0).
  gpupot.{sse,avx}.cpp, gpupot.gpu.cu, gpupot.metal.mm : + gpupot_range_
    fallback (full evaluation, copy the slice) so the shared energy2.f links
    in every backend; only reachable with internal MPI np>1, which no build
    of those backends wires up yet. True ranged GPU kernel = G2 work item.
  GPU2/mpi_nbody.f      : + NBODY_PHI_GATHER (1 Allgatherv, REGF_RANGE split,
    MPI_IN_PLACE); no-op stub in mpi_nbody_stub.f.
  GPU2/energy2.f        : NRANKS>1 -> GPUPOT_RANGE over the rank's
    NBODY_REGF_RANGE slice + NBODY_PHI_GATHER; else the original GPUPOT.
    The PHICOR/POT summation below is untouched and runs replicated in the
    original fixed order on identical gathered inputs -> bit-identical POT.

BIT-IDENTITY
  run_equiv.sh (13049-body BSE, per-rank dirs): PASS -- np1 (original GPUPOT
  path) == np2 == np4, all ranks. This directly proves gpupot_range == gpupot
  per particle, since np1 takes the old code path.
  N=5e4 attribution runs: np8 ADJUST/END RUN physics lines bit-identical to
  np1 at BOTH cadences. Block-step and ADJUST counts identical (control flow
  unchanged).

